; {$packrecords} and {$align} values that are not alignments (as Free
; Pascal's "illegal record alignment specifier"), and typed constants of
; records laid out with a field alignment (packed, {$packrecords}), which
; are their bytes, holding values they cannot (ansistrings, pointers).
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/packrecords/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:2:1: error: illegal record alignment '3': use 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, C, DEFAULT or NORMAL
; CHECK: errors.pas:3:1: error: illegal record alignment 'foo': use 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, C, DEFAULT or NORMAL
; CHECK: errors.pas:4:1: error: illegal record alignment '5': use 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, ON or OFF
; CHECK-NOT: error:

; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/packrecords/consts.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=CONSTS %s
; CONSTS: consts.pas:11:11: error: typed constants of packed records or records under {$packrecords} with values of type 'ansistring' are not supported yet
; CONSTS: consts.pas:12:11: error: typed constants of packed records or records under {$packrecords} with values of type 'pointer' are not supported yet
; CONSTS: consts.pas:14:15: error: typed constants of packed records or records under {$packrecords} with values of type 'ansistring' are not supported yet
; CONSTS-NOT: error:
